1205 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 705 0 R
/E ( When two robots request the same zone, the controller admits the one with the higher package priority. On a tie, the robot with fewer infractions wins; if still tied, R1 wins. A robot returning empty has priority 0.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1206 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3306 0 R
/E <4E33208520507265656D7074696F6E2E>
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1207 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 705 0 R
/E ( A robot occupying a zone must retreat to the adjacent Side Bay when a robot that wins over it under N2 requests that zone. Retreat is not a sanction: the robot keeps its delivery and may return when the zone is free.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1208 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3307 0 R
/E <4E34208520446561646C696E6520262053616E6374696F6E2E20>
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1209 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 705 0 R
/E (A robot with an active delivery that exceeds its tick deadline abandons it and goes to the adjacent Side Bay. The Fleet Manager increments its infraction counter and applies a fixed cooldown \(COOLDOWN ticks\) before the robot returns empty to a station for a new task.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
